<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en"><section class="case-intro"><span class="case-no">ARCHITECTURE STORY / 03</span><h1>Insurance moves to digital channels.</h1><p class="lede">Before omnichannel retail and SaaS, the problem was already the same: connect a new digital experience with systems that were never designed around the web.</p></section><div class="case-facts"><div><small>Period</small><strong>2005 — 2010</strong></div><div><small>Domain</small><strong>Insurance · Financial services</strong></div><div><small>Focus</small><strong>Online sales · Payments · Integration</strong></div></div><section class="case-body"><div class="prose"><h2>Digital was an integration problem.</h2><div><p>At Cruz del Sur I worked on digital insurance initiatives including online sales and payments, portal platforms, call-center/IVR capabilities and integrations with financial systems.</p><p>The work also included evolution of the application platform around WebSphere, connecting customer-facing capabilities with established enterprise systems.</p></div></div><div class="system-flow"><span class="node">Web / Portal</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node accent">Application platform</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">Insurance systems</span><span class="link">↔</span><span class="node">Financial services</span></div><div class="decision-list"><div class="decision"><b>01</b><strong>Expose services digitally</strong><p>Bring sales and payment capabilities to online channels without treating the web as an isolated front end.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>02</b><strong>Integrate channels</strong><p>Connect web, call-center/IVR and enterprise processes around the same business operation.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>03</b><strong>Evolve the platform</strong><p>Participate in WebSphere-based application platform evolution and enterprise integration.</p></div></div></section></BaseLayout>